      <data key="d1">"1 is a constant integer value repeatedly used in the student's matrix as elements, serving as a baseline for constructing the determinant with absolute values ≥1."&lt;SEP&gt;"The integer 1 appears repeatedly as a fixed element in the matrix, serving as a structural anchor in the student's solution. It represents a constant 'location' in the matrix grid that constrains the determinant's behavior and is critical to the error analysis."</data>
