    <node id="&quot;21-1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Event ID 21-1 refers to a recorded instance of a student's incorrect submission on October 13, 2024, at 20:23:27, related to the行列式 construction problem."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-468ecda2a7ffd84f7956eab9b179bd56</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;数值膨胀之美&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"‘数值膨胀之美’是该算法题的标题，象征通过将区间元素乘2（数值膨胀）来优化极差的解题过程，代表一次抽象的算法优化事件。"&lt;SEP&gt;"数值膨胀之美是本题的描述性标题，指代通过将数组中某区间元素乘以2实现数值扩张，从而优化极差的算法问题场景。"&lt;SEP&gt;"数值膨胀之美是该题目的标题，隐喻通过将区间元素乘以2（数值膨胀）来探索优化极差的巧妙解法。"&lt;SEP&gt;"数值膨胀之美是本题的标题，象征通过将数组元素乘以2（数值膨胀）来优化极差的算法问题，是题目背景和核心操作的隐喻表达。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29266653556f4758c4fbea2541c63207&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11c9647dca18b1c8953d3725e54e2230&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-802a483142e00c23622efad16d2e5519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3eac5a8ba5cac7de40889ced9fb5315</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECORD ID: 22-1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Record ID: 22-1 是该题目提交的唯一标识记录，包含错误分析和时间戳（2025-01-21 13:27:31），用于追踪学生答案的评估过程。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-11c9647dca18b1c8953d3725e54e2230</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;极差&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"极差是数组中最大值与最小值的差值，作为衡量数组数值分布离散程度的指标，是小红试图最小化的优化目标。"&lt;SEP&gt;"极差是数组的核心数学属性，定义为最大值减去最小值，是学生操作试图优化的目标指标。"&lt;SEP&gt;"极差是数组中最大值与最小值的差值，是小红希望最小化的量化目标，是本题算法问题的核心度量标准。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29266653556f4758c4fbea2541c63207&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11c9647dca18b1c8953d3725e54e2230&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-802a483142e00c23622efad16d2e5519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;乘以2操作&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"乘以2操作是指选择数组中一个非空区间，将其中所有元素值翻倍的唯一允许操作，是解题的关键动作。"&lt;SEP&gt;"乘以2操作是题目允许的唯一操作，指选择一个非空区间，将其所有元素值翻倍，用于调整数组极差。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-11c9647dca18b1c8953d3725e54e2230&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-802a483142e00c23622efad16d2e5519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;非空区间&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"非空区间指数组中连续的一个或多个元素组成的子序列，小红的操作是选择这样一个区间并将其中所有元素乘以2。"&lt;SEP&gt;"非空区间是数组中连续子序列的抽象概念，学生需选择其中一个执行乘以2操作，是解题策略的核心变量。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-11c9647dca18b1c8953d3725e54e2230&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-802a483142e00c23622efad16d2e5519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;排序&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"排序是学生程序中执行的步骤，将数组元素按升序排列，用于简化极差计算，但该步骤在本题中可能误导算法设计。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-11c9647dca18b1c8953d3725e54e2230</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;A[N] - A[1] * 2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"a[n] - a[1] * 2 是学生程序中错误计算的候选极差之一，错误地假设最小值翻倍后与最大值比较，忽略了其他可能的极差组合。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-11c9647dca18b1c8953d3725e54e2230</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;(A[N] - A[1]) * 2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"(a[n] - a[1]) * 2 是学生程序中另一个候选极差，错误地假设整个数组翻倍，而实际只能翻倍一个区间，导致逻辑错误。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-11c9647dca18b1c8953d3725e54e2230</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROGRAM SEGMENT 1/2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">Program Segment 1/2 is the first part of a student’s submitted C++ implementation aimed at solving the “好矩阵” (good matrix) transformation problem, which requires relocating all '1's in a binary matrix to the top-left quadrant using only adjacent swaps (horizontal and vertical). This segment is responsible for reading and initializing the input matrix, tracking the positions of '1's via a coordinate system defined by control variables (cnti, cntj), and recording each swap operation in a vector for output. The implementation employs a greedy, interval-expansion strategy, attempting to sequentially move each '1' toward the top-left corner through nested loops that iterate over the matrix.

While the structural framework is fundamentally sound—correctly parsing input, maintaining state for target positions, and capturing the sequence of operations—the program contains critical logical flaws that prevent reliable execution. These include incorrect reset and update logic for cnti and cntj, defective loop sequencing that misaligns the traversal order, and erroneous assumptions about how matrix positions should be updated after each swap. Additional implementation defects include the random generation of matrix dimensions n and m (instead of reading them from input), inaccurate counting mechanisms (cnt), and a lack of validation to confirm whether the target configuration has been achieved. These errors lead to incorrect output and partial correctness, as reflected by a contest score of 40/100.

Although one description ambiguously references an unrelated problem involving diagonal prefix sums and grid transposition for computing maximum monsters defeated by Dragon’s Breath, and another incorrectly associates the segment with a permutation checker problem using persistent segment trees, these are inconsistent with the overwhelming consensus across all inputs, including Chinese-language sources, which confirm the task is unequivocally a matrix transformation via adjacent swaps. The reference to “双生数组” (twin array), median-based sorting, or string “可爱度” (cuteness) generation further corroborates these as misattributions or noise. Therefore, Program Segment 1/2 is best understood as a well-intentioned but flawed coordinate-aware solution: its conceptual approach aligns with the problem’s requirements, but its implementation errors—particularly in state management and swap sequencing—significantly undermine its effectiveness.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a0e68ffe11c5d605b2d172bc117a660&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eeffa4db6e2444dac981d2f6e46c8e68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5e545f02779dfb717361dfc31cb72c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ec34f58c7576beef3e1ee627c114a25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc322d7318797c103f604c41177f547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c02916b7b0e5a87f92d544844a99ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82ae2ff0e583348ae265216d143270fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47e1da39547e4d5d5cdafb2530c061c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-466772e1ad2cb9b8fdd70bf09c71858c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad8afc7ac300d86b72e962805041fa5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24e91156da41d8c127cfcd98fd99217c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2a57305752e3a687103dd58dbee53bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f83dfef3345c73ed407093c9749130b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de530eec1b33d2199269b22b88bb1c32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f089790696661ee6abceff90f9924d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7638980c6db214619f264bda3c98a5b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e8858aadef99b81cf3431326cb24cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2aa783b90d0126e6fe65518c125bef47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-504efc1d29aab22b90705499f57173fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66aa472cb9a249d5511f69ff4cdc9520&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c5bdeaa2e5f505a00838eed99bce2dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46766da85f9f13835e435950173174a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3eac5a8ba5cac7de40889ced9fb5315&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-411bbe91994001030c7a545311f4d2a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0be1ff21d6f00384f294e712dc03c7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bbc06444b81cde07bd3f70e96886225&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8639879bd177c95139010b9025b24c97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d45a376c5f8e29b656fb8024a9e1fab6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8796025571904280b91872c5eb3f6610</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ERROR DESCRIPTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Error Description is the feedback on the Student Program's performance, indicating partial correctness with a score of 18.75%, highlighting a flaw in the logic or implementation of the checker."&lt;SEP&gt;The "ERROR DESCRIPTION" is a formal, structured diagnostic and evaluation mechanism used in automated grading systems to identify, document, and analyze failures in student submissions for the “双生数组” (twin array) transformation problem. It is triggered when a student’s algorithm produces output that deviates from the expected correct solution—specifically, when the generated matrix fails to satisfy two essential conditions of a “好矩阵” (good matrix): (1) equal frequency of all elements across the entire matrix, and (2) precise placement of all ‘1’s exclusively within the top-left n/2 × n/2 quadrant. 

This mechanism is not a simple pass/fail indicator but a detailed, evidence-based record that captures the exact nature of algorithmic errors, enabling targeted instructional feedback and student remediation. Each ERROR DESCRIPTION is uniquely logged with a record ID and timestamp, creating a precise audit trail of individual submission failures. Examples of documented events include record IDs 106-1 (2025-02-08), 107-1 (2025-02-08 16:35:20), 105-1 (2025-02-08 16:31:58), 103-1 (2025-02-08 16:25:19), 99-1 (2025-02-08), 95-1 (2025-02-08 14:13:08), 80-1 (2025-02-06 14:03:57), 79-1 (2025-02-06 13:54:37), 62-1 (2025-01-23 13:49:22), 61-1 (2025-01-23 13:47:29), 59-2 (2025-01-21 17:56:06), 54-1 (2025-01-21 17:46:38), 54-2, 44-</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fbb166f8ec0a1178f2d878ecaab5e98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e2289b634557fb82c8cd29d3444ae10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29764514e79d905f57239a2bf826b46d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2d77cdcffc291f16acc127cdfe41569&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5df2edc3d03ec6c5e1b9a6d2ff7905f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eeffa4db6e2444dac981d2f6e46c8e68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8571d78ef0982dfe0d6ef86e585cbe98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a0e68ffe11c5d605b2d172bc117a660&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5e545f02779dfb717361dfc31cb72c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ec34f58c7576beef3e1ee627c114a25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7907aaf6e77e8266bb40e1c8a136bf60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c02916b7b0e5a87f92d544844a99ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82ae2ff0e583348ae265216d143270fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-985dca88cf19334aa6bccf195ded5fbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47e1da39547e4d5d5cdafb2530c061c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06373e967b229fd23b64bfbbc0860861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fe6cf8d6835af29afa5ade64370e360&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-466772e1ad2cb9b8fdd70bf09c71858c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad8afc7ac300d86b72e962805041fa5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffffe6b4389bb3df97140e17e088aa9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24e91156da41d8c127cfcd98fd99217c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e118fc6033f61b8968a68a6cbe21cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13a9ab5634b62de5516cbb77c8616b93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb748d740807dc942d42a2dc4f25d05d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2a57305752e3a687103dd58dbee53bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b7bfa15e059051e591b4500f150f4b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b0b936b6b647a37d956fdf66cd57a12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70a2665d10418a7ca4b53ae850057cff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f83dfef3345c73ed407093c9749130b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de530eec1b33d2199269b22b88bb1c32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ae1fc917022eddc74e2fec3c8d34bb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c43422d516179991d5c796063c71f443&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7638980c6db214619f264bda3c98a5b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1446a315ea545061645e2e34bdaaffae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f089790696661ee6abceff90f9924d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2aa783b90d0126e6fe65518c125bef47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-504efc1d29aab22b90705499f57173fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e5949ffd4dcb4848ea0732665205b59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ef1f71a373fc41a4b61f69de3413bf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-264071873a8220efc52cdb3c6f973f1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8796025571904280b91872c5eb3f6610&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54e2ed195b50756e6f2448b5f990c4b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c79d0a874a6ba47efd4742ec70c1e196&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66aa472cb9a249d5511f69ff4cdc9520&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c04c2481dfa06e8cc96fafb3eb40ca4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2c34d00a1cb1d7916cefb78fbc43896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c5bdeaa2e5f505a00838eed99bce2dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91d5ad5a52520d2ee66b7e8855842a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46766da85f9f13835e435950173174a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4655c44a0c410e0c718d92b308d741b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3eac5a8ba5cac7de40889ced9fb5315&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f02234c0d5217769809ae214a58779b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d353b59db67cab15706b3f74c4fa457&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e307f6e0f75e0c72f6c263b74efaa1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0be1ff21d6f00384f294e712dc03c7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9bb8ae3fef264eb1654019ea7fdabc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d887a2fa6fff76122dbcba92f32c0d9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa7949c55def1b07cb22840b26c2d9a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a6cf2c1b884640bd458e20b236729e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bbc06444b81cde07bd3f70e96886225&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63d7c8c700f1653b2de9c2e270fef6e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8639879bd177c95139010b9025b24c97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d45a376c5f8e29b656fb8024a9e1fab6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f24131db9a2e06f7a88e10188152d99d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7fa52e5b330629e1cee02304480f542&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe255a1fe76c6cdfb705f9ea60c587de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7effc3a8936d5e21e04e38b0253505c0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECORD ID: 23-1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Record ID: 23-1 is a system log entry timestamped 2025-01-21 14:03:26, used to track and reference the specific submission and evaluation of the student’s program in an automated grading or learning system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3eac5a8ba5cac7de40889ced9fb5315</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INT_MAX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"INT_MAX is a constant from C++'s &lt;climits&gt; library, used in the student program to represent the maximum possible integer value for initializing minimum arrays and the answer variable. It serves as a sentinel value in the algorithm."&lt;SEP&gt;"INT_MAX 是C++中表示整数最大值的常量，在学生程序中用于初始化和边界处理，代表数值上界，影响最大值和最小值的计算逻辑。"&lt;SEP&gt;"INT_MAX 是 C++ 中表示整数最大值的常量，用于初始化最小敲碎数 Min，是程序中用于算法优化的技术实现细节。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-802a483142e00c23622efad16d2e5519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0e2ac3fe25900f76cfe73eedcd9570d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3eac5a8ba5cac7de40889ced9fb5315</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STD::VECTOR&lt;INT&gt;&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"std::vector&lt;int&gt; is a C++ standard library container used in the student program to store the input array, doubled array, and prefix/suffix minimum arrays. It enables dynamic memory management and indexed access."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3eac5a8ba5cac7de40889ced9fb5315</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STD::MAP&lt;INT, INT&gt;&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"std::map&lt;int, int&gt; is a sorted associative container used in the student program to record the leftmost (L) and rightmost (R) positions of each unique array value for interval boundary calculation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3eac5a8ba5cac7de40889ced9fb5315</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;L[A[I]]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"L[a[i]] is a map entry storing the leftmost (minimum) index where value a[i] appears in the array, used to determine the boundaries of intervals that include specific values after doubling."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3eac5a8ba5cac7de40889ced9fb5315</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;R[A[I]]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"R[a[i]] is a map entry storing the rightmost (maximum) index where value a[i] appears in the array, used alongside L[a[i]] to define the span of intervals to double."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3eac5a8ba5cac7de40889ced9fb5315</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIN_PRE[I]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Min_pre[i] is a prefix minimum array where each element stores the minimum value from the start of the array up to index i, used to efficiently compute the minimum outside a doubled interval."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3eac5a8ba5cac7de40889ced9fb5315</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIN_SUF[I]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Min_suf[i] is a suffix minimum array where each element stores the minimum value from index i to the end of the array, used to compute the global minimum when a middle segment is doubled."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3eac5a8ba5cac7de40889ced9fb5315</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;区间乘2操作&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"区间乘2操作是小红计划执行的唯一一次操作，即选择数组中的一个非空连续子区间，将其中所有元素乘以2，以期最小化整个数组的极差。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29266653556f4758c4fbea2541c63207</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;错误描述&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"错误描述是针对学生程序的评估结果，指出其输出与预期答案存在差异，表明程序逻辑存在缺陷，未能正确实现‘好矩阵’的构造目标。"&lt;SEP&gt;"错误描述是针对学生程序输出结果不正确的分析记录，指出其答案与正确答案存在差异，是本次问题评估的关键事件。"&lt;SEP&gt;"错误描述记录了学生程序的两个主要问题：答案不正确，且与正确答案存在差异，表明程序逻辑存在缺陷。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29266653556f4758c4fbea2541c63207&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58fc77dbcd0a97d49a184217f891dcb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47baadad1b80a9eb7ea15b9cd824968b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECORD ID: 23-2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Record ID: 23-2 是该问题提交的唯一标识，记录了错误发生的时间戳（2025-01-21 14:03:26），用于追踪和复现问题。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29266653556f4758c4fbea2541c63207</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;排列构造问题&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"排列构造问题是一个算法挑战事件，要求构造一个满足区间约束的 1~n 排列，是学生程序试图解决的核心任务。"&lt;SEP&gt;"排列构造问题是一个算法挑战事件，要求构造一个满足区间约束的 1~n 排列，是学生程序试图解决的核心任务，且被记录为错误解答的案例。"&lt;SEP&gt;"排列构造问题是一个算法挑战事件，要求构造一个长度为 n 的排列，使得第 i 个元素落在给定区间 [l_i, r_i] 内，是学生程序试图解决的核心任务。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e99c195bf139756748ff95a63861cbef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6dde8d5dace842a3db295bc3a2b69c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab26ec20fcd79dc385eb33e508c23dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1~N&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1~n represents the range of integers from 1 to n, which must be used exactly once to form a valid permutation; it is a conceptual geographic range of values in the problem space."&lt;SEP&gt;"1~n 表示从 1 到 n 的整数范围，是排列构造问题中元素取值的全局约束区间，属于算法问题中的数值空间定义。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f6dde8d5dace842a3db295bc3a2b69c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab26ec20fcd79dc385eb33e508c23dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;[L_I,R_I]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"[l_i,r_i] 是第 i 个位置元素的取值区间约束，每个 i 对应一个独立的数值范围，是排列构造问题中的核心局部约束条件。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ab26ec20fcd79dc385eb33e508c23dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T{INT L, R, ID}&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T 是学生程序中定义的结构体类型，用于存储每个位置的左边界 l、右边界 r 和原始索引 id，是实现贪心算法的数据结构基础。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ab26ec20fcd79dc385eb33e508c23dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANS[M]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ans[M] is an array in the student program that stores the final assigned values for each position in the permutation, indexed by original position id."&lt;SEP&gt;"ans[M] 是学生程序中用于存储最终排列结果的数组，按原始索引 id 赋值，是输出结果的关键数据结构。"&lt;SEP&gt;"ans[M] is an array in the student program used to store the final assigned values for each position in the permutation, indexed by original position id.""&lt;SEP&gt;"ans[M] 是学生程序中用于存储最终排列结果的数组，按原始索引 id 赋值，是输出合法排列的载体。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-512301a13a22c9eae82f981e0542065a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e99c195bf139756748ff95a63861cbef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab26ec20fcd79dc385eb33e508c23dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cfc0f9443b7ad1fe6055d788e835294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STD::SORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"std::sort is a C++ standard library function used in the student program to sort intervals by their left bounds, a key step in the greedy algorithm approach."&lt;SEP&gt;"std::sort is the C++ standard library function used in the student program to sort constraints by their left bound l, then by right bound r, to enable greedy assignment."&lt;SEP&gt;"std::sort 是 C++ 标准库函数，学生程序中用于按 l 升序、r 升序对区间进行排序，是贪心策略实施的前提步骤。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f6dde8d5dace842a3db295bc3a2b69c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab26ec20fcd79dc385eb33e508c23dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cfc0f9443b7ad1fe6055d788e835294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;L = 1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"'l = 1' initializes the smallest available integer to be assigned in the greedy algorithm, starting from 1 as required by permutation constraints.""&lt;SEP&gt;"l = 1 initializes the smallest available integer for greedy assignment, which is incremented after each successful assignment in the student program."&lt;SEP&gt;"l = 1 是学生程序中用于贪心分配的当前可用最小整数，初始为 1，随分配递增，代表全局可用数值的游标。"&lt;SEP&gt;"l = 1 是贪心算法中当前可分配的最小整数值，从 1 开始递增，用于尝试填充每个区间约束。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-512301a13a22c9eae82f981e0542065a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e99c195bf139756748ff95a63861cbef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab26ec20fcd79dc385eb33e508c23dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cfc0f9443b7ad1fe6055d788e835294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1 \SIM N&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"'1 \sim n' represents the range of integer values from 1 to n, which are the only valid elements allowed in a valid permutation; it defines the universal domain for the problem.""&lt;SEP&gt;"1 \sim n 表示排列中允许使用的整数范围，即从 1 到 n 的连续整数集合，是构造合法排列的数值域约束。"&lt;SEP&gt;"1 \sim n denotes the set of integers from 1 to n, which form the valid elements of any permutation in this problem."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b590abbdea60c545ca54c73ea12cc6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e99c195bf139756748ff95a63861cbef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dae03b8ab8904bfd565e3a28acd596fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;井然有序之窗&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"井然有序之窗是该问题的标题或主题名称，代表一个需要构造满足区间限制的排列的算法挑战事件。"&lt;SEP&gt;"井然有序之窗是该问题的标题或主题名称，象征着在给定区间约束下构造有序排列的挑战性任务，代表一种算法问题的抽象情境。"&lt;SEP&gt;"井然有序之窗是该问题的标题，象征着通过正确构造排列来满足区间约束的逻辑挑战，代表一个需要解决的算法事件。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-512301a13a22c9eae82f981e0542065a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cfc0f9443b7ad1fe6055d788e835294&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b590abbdea60c545ca54c73ea12cc6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;[L_I, R_I]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"'[l_i, r_i]' is the constrained range for the i-th element in the permutation, specifying valid boundaries each value must fall within; it is a key input constraint for the problem.""&lt;SEP&gt;"[l_i, r_i] denotes the inclusive range constraint for the i-th element in the permutation, defining valid values each position can take, central to the problem’s logic."&lt;SEP&gt;"[l_i, r_i] 是第 i 个位置允许的数值区间约束，每个 i 对应一个独立的整数范围，是构造合法排列的关键限制条件。"&lt;SEP&gt;"[l_i, r_i] denotes the inclusive range of valid values for the i-th element in the permutation, defining constraints that each position must satisfy; it is a mathematical boundary region in the problem’s constraint space."&lt;SEP&gt;"[l_i, r_i] 是第 i 个位置允许放置元素的数值区间约束，每个 i 对应一个独立的范围限制，是构造合法排列的核心输入条件。"&lt;SEP&gt;"[l_i, r_i] denotes the inclusive integer interval within which each element a_i of the sequence is independently and uniformly randomly generated, serving as a range constraint for randomness."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e99c195bf139756748ff95a63861cbef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6dde8d5dace842a3db295bc3a2b69c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cfc0f9443b7ad1fe6055d788e835294&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a6cf2c1b884640bd458e20b236729e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b590abbdea60c545ca54c73ea12cc6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-512301a13a22c9eae82f981e0542065a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STD::CIN / STD::COUT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"std::cin 和 std::cout 是 C++ 标准输入输出流，用于读取 n、l_i、r_i 和输出结果，是程序与外部交互的核心组件。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b590abbdea60c545ca54c73ea12cc6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRUCT T&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"struct T 是学生定义的数据结构，用于封装每个位置的左边界 l、右边界 r 和原始索引 id，是算法逻辑中管理区间约束的基础单元。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b590abbdea60c545ca54c73ea12cc6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INT ANS[M]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"int ans[M] 是用于存储排列结果的数组，其中 ans[a[i].id] = l 表示将值 l 分配给第 i 个位置，是算法输出的关键数据结构。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b590abbdea60c545ca54c73ea12cc6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;#DEFINE INT LONG LONG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"#define int long long 是宏定义，将 int 类型重定义为 long long，用于避免大数溢出，反映学生对输入规模可能较大的预判。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b590abbdea60c545ca54c73ea12cc6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;3E5 +7&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"3e5 +7 是数组 M 的大小上限，表示程序设计支持最多 300,007 个元素的输入，是内存分配的数值约束。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b590abbdea60c545ca54c73ea12cc6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1 ~ N&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1 ~ n 表示排列中允许使用的整数范围，即从 1 到 n 的连续整数集合，是构造排列的数值空间约束。"&lt;SEP&gt;"The set of integers from 1 to n, which must each appear exactly once in a valid permutation, forming the universal domain of solution values."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-512301a13a22c9eae82f981e0542065a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cfc0f9443b7ad1fe6055d788e835294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A global counter variable used to assign unique node IDs in the persistent segment tree implementation, incrementing with each new node creation."&lt;SEP&gt;"T is a global counter tracking the total number of segment tree nodes created during the persistent tree construction."&lt;SEP&gt;"T is a struct defined in the student program to encapsulate the left bound, right bound, and original index of each interval, serving as a data structure for processing constraints."&lt;SEP&gt;"T is a struct type defined in the student program to encapsulate the left bound (l), right bound (r), and original index (id) of each constraint for sorting and assignment."&lt;SEP&gt;"T 是学生程序中定义的结构体类型，用于存储每个位置的区间 [l, r] 和原始索引 id，是算法数据组织的核心单元。"&lt;SEP&gt;"T is a variable representing the number of test cases in the student's program, used to loop through multiple matrix inputs for processing."&lt;SEP&gt;"T is an integer variable in the student's program representing the number of test cases to be processed, initialized to 1 and decremented in a loop."&lt;SEP&gt;"t 是题目要求构造的目标字符串，长度为 n，仅由小写字母组成，且其可爱度必须恰好等于 m。"&lt;SEP&gt;"T is the number of test cases in the student program, read from input and used to loop through multiple instances of the problem."&lt;SEP&gt;"T是学生程序中表示测试用例数量的整数变量，用于控制循环次数。"&lt;SEP&gt;"T is a variable in the student's program representing the number of test cases, used to control the loop that calls the solve() function. It is implied to be an input provided by the problem setter or judge system."&lt;SEP&gt;"T is a variable in the student program representing the number of test cases, used to control the loop that calls the solve() function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-180c6e0fe94889fc71026468d48a172f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e2289b634557fb82c8cd29d3444ae10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34b609ebf637b7a586a64207000b2d2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6dde8d5dace842a3db295bc3a2b69c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc322d7318797c103f604c41177f547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cfc0f9443b7ad1fe6055d788e835294&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bbd9f3652366c894d3ef5e4694e35b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dae03b8ab8904bfd565e3a28acd596fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-512301a13a22c9eae82f981e0542065a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31863a3502540c31035499a1b63c97c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79af8c07e093eeaf2a8b54738698e7af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e118fc6033f61b8968a68a6cbe21cd8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STD::CIN &gt;&gt; N&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"std::cin &gt;&gt; n is the input operation that reads the permutation length n from standard input, initiating the problem-solving process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5cfc0f9443b7ad1fe6055d788e835294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STD::CIN &gt;&gt; L &gt;&gt; R&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"std::cin &gt;&gt; l &gt;&gt; r reads the range constraints [l_i, r_i] for each position i, forming the core input data for the problem."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5cfc0f9443b7ad1fe6055d788e835294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\{2,3,1,5,4\}&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"'\{2,3,1,5,4\}' is an example of a valid permutation of length 5, used to illustrate correct output format and element uniqueness.""</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e99c195bf139756748ff95a63861cbef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\{1,2,2\}&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"'\{1,2,2\}' is an invalid permutation due to duplicate elements, used as a counterexample to emphasize the uniqueness constraint in permutations.""</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e99c195bf139756748ff95a63861cbef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\{1,3,4\}&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"'\{1,3,4\}' is an invalid permutation because it omits numbers from the 1~n range and includes out-of-range values, illustrating violation of the permutation definition.""</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e99c195bf139756748ff95a63861cbef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T{INT L, R, ID;}&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T is a struct definition in the student’s C++ code used to store the left bound, right bound, and original index of each constraint interval for sorting and assignment.""</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e99c195bf139756748ff95a63861cbef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STD::SORT(A + 1, A + 1 + N, [](T A, T B) { RETURN A.L &lt; B.L ? A.L &lt; B.L : A.R &lt; B.R; });&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This sorting step in the student program orders intervals by increasing left bound, then right bound, to enable greedy assignment — a core algorithmic strategy in the solution attempt.""</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e99c195bf139756748ff95a63861cbef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IF(L &gt;= A[I].L &amp;&amp; L &lt;= A[I].R) ANS[A[I].ID] = L, L++;&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This conditional assignment is the core greedy logic of the student program, attempting to assign the smallest available integer l to the current interval if feasible, then incrementing l.""</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e99c195bf139756748ff95a63861cbef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IF(L &gt; N) { ... } ELSE STD::COUT &lt;&lt; -1;&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This final check determines whether a complete valid permutation was constructed (l &gt; n) or if assignment failed (l &lt;= n), outputting the result or -1 accordingly.""</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e99c195bf139756748ff95a63861cbef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANS[]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ans[] is an array in the student program used to store the final assigned value for each position in the permutation, indexed by the original position id."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f6dde8d5dace842a3db295bc3a2b69c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STD::SORT(A + 1, A + 1 + N)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"std::sort(a + 1, a + 1 + n) 是学生程序中对区间约束按左端点排序的事件，是贪心策略启动的关键步骤。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-512301a13a22c9eae82f981e0542065a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;L &gt;= A[I].FIRST.FIRST &amp;&amp; L &lt;= A[I].FIRST.SECOND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"该条件判断当前最小可用值 l 是否落在第 i 个区间的 [l_i, r_i] 范围内，是贪心分配是否成功的决策事件。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-512301a13a22c9eae82f981e0542065a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANS[A[I].SECOND] = L, L++&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"该操作将当前最小可用值 l 分配给原始位置 a[i].second，并递增 l，是算法核心的赋值与推进事件。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-512301a13a22c9eae82f981e0542065a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;L &gt; N&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"l &gt; n 是判断是否成功构造完整排列的终止条件，若 l 超过 n 说明所有值都被成功分配，否则输出 -1。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-512301a13a22c9eae82f981e0542065a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;A[1] * 2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"a[1] * 2 是数组最小元素翻倍后的值，在学生程序中被反复用于计算新的全局最小值，是极差计算的关键候选值。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-802a483142e00c23622efad16d2e5519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;A[I] * 2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"a[i] * 2 是数组中第i个元素翻倍后的值，在循环中用于更新当前可能的最大值，是极差优化过程中的核心变量。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-802a483142e00c23622efad16d2e5519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;A[I + 1]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"a[i + 1] 是数组中第i+1个原始元素（未翻倍），在学生程序中被用作候选最小值，用于与a[1] * 2比较以确定新的全局最小值。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-802a483142e00c23622efad16d2e5519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;小苯&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"小苯是一个学生或参与者，面对一个涉及数组和位运算的算法问题，需要计算满足 a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j) 的元素对数量。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小苯是题目中的主角，获得一个由n个整数构成的数组，并试图计算满足a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j)的元素对的数量。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小苯是题目中的主角，拿到一个由n个整数构成的数组，并试图计算满足a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j)的元素对的数量。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小苯是题目中的主角，面对一个包含n个整数的数组，试图计算满足a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j)的元素对的数量。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小苯是题目中的主角，负责解决一个关于数组中元素异或与最大公约数关系的编程问题。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54e2ed195b50756e6f2448b5f990c4b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9bb8ae3fef264eb1654019ea7fdabc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b7bfa15e059051e591b4500f150f4b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91d5ad5a52520d2ee66b7e8855842a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f831b89c29a24b6f937f910e69eb76a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OI-WIKI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"OI-Wiki 是一个提供信息学竞赛相关知识的在线资源平台，被引用为位运算知识的参考资料。"&lt;SEP&gt;"OI-Wiki 是一个提供信息学竞赛相关知识的在线资源平台，被引用作为位运算知识的参考资料。"&lt;SEP&gt;"OI-Wiki是一个提供信息学竞赛相关知识的在线资源平台，文中被引用为位运算知识的参考资料，网址为https://oi-wiki.org/math/bit/#%E4%B8%8E%E6%88%96%E5%BC%82%E6%88%96。"&lt;SEP&gt;"OI-Wiki是一个提供信息学竞赛相关知识的在线资源平台，被引用为位运算知识的参考资料，网址为https://oi-wiki.org/math/bit/#%E4%B8%8E%E6%88%96%E5%BC%82%E6%88%96。"&lt;SEP&gt;"OI-Wiki是一个提供信息学竞赛相关知识的在线资源平台，被引用作为位运算知识的参考资料，网址为https://oi-wiki.org/math/bit/#%E4%B8%8E%E6%88%96%E5%BC%82%E6%88%96。"&lt;SEP&gt;"OI-Wiki是一个提供信息学竞赛相关知识的在线资源平台，被引用为位运算知识的参考资料。"&lt;SEP&gt;"OI-Wiki是一个提供信息学竞赛相关知识的在线资源平台，被引用为位运算知识的参考资料，网址为https://oi-wiki.org/math/bit/。"&lt;SEP&gt;"OI-Wiki是一个提供算法竞赛相关知识的在线资源平台，被引用为位运算知识的参考资料，网址为https://oi-wiki.org/math/bit/。"&lt;SEP&gt;"OI-Wiki是一个提供信息学竞赛相关知识的在线资源平台，被引用为位运算知识的参考资料。"&lt;SEP&gt;"OI-Wiki是一个提供信息学竞赛相关知识的在线资源组织，被引用为位运算知识的参考资料。"&lt;SEP&gt;"OI-Wiki是一个提供信息学竞赛相关知识的在线资源平台，被引用为位运算知识的参考资料。"</data>
