    </node>
    <node id="&quot;牛可乐&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"牛可乐是题目中的出题者，定义了字符串的‘可爱度’概念，并提出了关于是否存在满足特定条件字符串的问题。"&lt;SEP&gt;牛可乐是多个算法问题的提出者与题目定义者，在离散结构与字符串算法两个方向上均提出了具有理论深度与算法挑战性的问题。在字符串算法领域，牛可乐定义了“可爱度”这一核心概念：对于一个字符串，其“可爱度”为最大的整数k，使得存在一个长度为k的连续子串，与一个由至少两段不相邻非空子串构成的、长度同样为k的不连续子序列完全相等；基于此定义，牛可乐进一步提出了判定是否存在满足该条件的字符串的算法问题。在离散结构领域，牛可乐独立提出了另一个原创性问题——砖块矩阵问题，其中他定义了“蓝色极大连通块”的概念，并要求计算使特定蓝色连通块掉落所需敲碎的最少灰色砖块数量，该问题聚焦于网格结构中的连通性分析与最小破坏策略的优化。综上所述，牛可乐作为出题者，其贡献覆盖了字符串模式匹配与网格连通性控制两大算法方向，均以精巧的定义和深刻的算法挑战性著称。</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e2d77cdcffc291f16acc127cdfe41569&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae077aa7a5a85409843a4ac34869acd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8571d78ef0982dfe0d6ef86e585cbe98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61548360973c5cefdc1038d32bf69e3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67a35ea6ed4e42eb7c4874b218ee041d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82ae2ff0e583348ae265216d143270fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca7b7c2c9549b0f15b3ed9c255cd57c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d58149e2705f5337a0bc1e192ab33a56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2da9ecfa854ec125c90cf41bc3e549e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bcd1771d7e55d80f714bbc3d88370bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7638980c6db214619f264bda3c98a5b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-435d0b64fef9c51a64d020305df4c4a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e8858aadef99b81cf3431326cb24cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cb4bd7875d45de235db605ada816662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0e2ac3fe25900f76cfe73eedcd9570d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31863a3502540c31035499a1b63c97c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79af8c07e093eeaf2a8b54738698e7af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f71a436c68bda6c051ade04f84d6c77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34b609ebf637b7a586a64207000b2d2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd5a87d368619780b9c83a36a26e8d95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;蓝色极大连通块&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"蓝色极大连通块是指在矩阵中由四连通的蓝色砖块构成的最大连通区域，不包含灰色砖块，其是否掉落取决于是否与灰色砖块共边，是问题的核心计算目标。"&lt;SEP&gt;"蓝色极大连通块是指由四连通的蓝色砖块组成的最大连通区域，不包含灰色砖块，其是否掉落取决于是否与灰色砖块共边，是题目中核心的计算目标。"&lt;SEP&gt;"蓝色极大连通块是指由四连通的蓝色砖块组成的最大连通区域，不包含灰色砖块，其是否掉落取决于是否与灰色砖块共边，是题目中需要分析和计算的核心对象。"&lt;SEP&gt;"蓝色极大连通块是指由四连通的蓝色砖块组成的最大连通区域，不包含灰色砖块，其是否掉落取决于是否与灰色砖块共边，是题目中的核心问题对象。"&lt;SEP&gt;"蓝色极大连通块是指由四连通的蓝色砖块组成的最大连通区域，不包含灰色砖块，其是否掉落取决于是否与灰色砖块共边，是题目中需要分析和计算的核心对象。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae077aa7a5a85409843a4ac34869acd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61548360973c5cefdc1038d32bf69e3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bcd1771d7e55d80f714bbc3d88370bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0e2ac3fe25900f76cfe73eedcd9570d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e8858aadef99b81cf3431326cb24cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;灰色砖块&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"灰色砖块代表可被敲碎的砖块，在题目中作为障碍物或需移除的元素，用于隔离或触发蓝色极大连通块的掉落，是解决问题的关键操作对象。"&lt;SEP&gt;"灰色砖块代表可被敲碎的砖块，在题目中作为障碍物，其敲碎数量决定蓝色极大连通块能否掉落，是解题的关键操作对象。"&lt;SEP&gt;"灰色砖块是可被敲碎的砖块，用于隔离或破坏蓝色极大连通块，其敲碎数量是问题求解的关键变量，代表一种操作资源。"&lt;SEP&gt;"灰色砖块是矩阵中可被敲碎的砖块，用于隔离或移除蓝色极大连通块，是计算最少敲碎数量的关键对象。"&lt;SEP&gt;"灰色砖块是矩阵中可被敲碎的砖块，用于隔离或使蓝色极大连通块掉落，是计算最少敲碎数量的关键对象。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae077aa7a5a85409843a4ac34869acd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61548360973c5cefdc1038d32bf69e3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bcd1771d7e55d80f714bbc3d88370bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0e2ac3fe25900f76cfe73eedcd9570d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e8858aadef99b81cf3431326cb24cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;蓝色砖块&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"蓝色砖块是不可敲碎的砖块，以蓝色斜线绘制，构成蓝色极大连通块的唯一组成部分，其连通性决定了问题的结构复杂度。"&lt;SEP&gt;"蓝色砖块是矩阵中不可敲碎的砖块，通过四连通形成蓝色极大连通块，是分析掉落条件的基础元素。"&lt;SEP&gt;"蓝色砖块是矩阵中不可敲碎的砖块，以蓝色斜线表示，构成蓝色极大连通块的基本单元，其连通性决定块的结构。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bcd1771d7e55d80f714bbc3d88370bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0e2ac3fe25900f76cfe73eedcd9570d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e8858aadef99b81cf3431326cb24cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;(I,J)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"(i,j) is a coordinate system used to identify positions on the 3x3 tic-tac-toe board, where i denotes the row (1 to 3 from top to bottom) and j denotes the column (1 to 3 from left to right)."&lt;SEP&gt;The coordinate system (i,j) is a fundamental spatial reference used to identify and locate individual cells within an n-row by m-column grid map, where i represents the row index (numbered from top to bottom) and j represents the column index (numbered from left to right). This system serves as the core mathematical notation for precisely defining the physical position of each brick or cell in the grid. It is essential for describing the spatial relationships between different types of bricks—such as blue and gray bricks—and for analyzing their connectivity, forming the basis for identifying connected components and developing strategies for brick removal or manipulation. Additionally, (i,j) underpins critical game mechanics, including the placement of monsters and the targeting of abilities such as Dragon’s Breath, making it indispensable for both structural representation and dynamic interaction within the grid-based environment. All descriptions consistently align on the orientation and function of (i,j), with no contradictions present.&lt;SEP&gt;"(i,j) is a coordinate system used to identify positions on the 3x3 tic-tac-toe board, where i is the row (1 to 3 from top to bottom) and j is the column (1 to 3 from left to right)."&lt;SEP&gt;"(i,j) is a coordinate system used to identify positions on the 3x3 tic-tac-toe board, where i is the row (1 to 3 from top to bottom) and j is the column (1 to 3 from left to right)."&lt;SEP&gt;"(i,j) is the coordinate system used to identify each cell in the 3x3 grid, where i is the row (1 to 3 from top to bottom) and j is the column (1 to 3 from left to right)."&lt;SEP&gt;"(i,j) is a coordinate system used to identify positions on the 3x3 tic-tac-toe board, where i is the row (1 to 3) and j is the column (1 to 3). It defines the spatial structure of the game state."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae077aa7a5a85409843a4ac34869acd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61548360973c5cefdc1038d32bf69e3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d793d3b341bfc53e485a1d35351f539&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0414d324dc902fa7bfe392b580d12b0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bcd1771d7e55d80f714bbc3d88370bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d177fa42f88e3250bf9921ff21987ec2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-325b730cedcf46c053439807511ce0ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0e2ac3fe25900f76cfe73eedcd9570d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9096db2ee9b817fdd4447c67ca4e24c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41bb705f581ef523c90424ea77cfe827&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ab3ebf5f1287dbbf9a2ec35fad95eea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64cb9d6867521174d17ba3213df66180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e8858aadef99b81cf3431326cb24cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-411bbe91994001030c7a545311f4d2a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89dd6bd1e7fef4152822627f117d0a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-031bf50845b77cce37dae6bb7e48b3a8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N \TIMES M 矩阵&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"n \times m 矩阵是题目中砖块的二维排列结构，由 n 行 m 列的砖块组成，是整个问题的物理和逻辑基础。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18e8858aadef99b81cf3431326cb24cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;四连通&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"四连通是指上下左右四个方向的相邻关系，用于定义蓝色砖块之间是否属于同一个连通块，是识别蓝色极大连通块的核心规则。"&lt;SEP&gt;"四连通是指上下左右四个方向的相邻关系，用于定义蓝色砖块之间是否属于同一连通块，是识别蓝色极大连通块的算法基础。"&lt;SEP&gt;"四连通是指上下左右四个方向的相邻关系，用于定义蓝色砖块是否属于同一连通块，是判断极大连通块的核心规则。"&lt;SEP&gt;"四连通是指上下左右四个方向的相邻关系，用于定义蓝色砖块之间是否属于同一连通块，是识别蓝色极大连通块的算法基础。"&lt;SEP&gt;"四连通是指上下左右四个方向的相邻关系，用于定义蓝色砖块是否属于同一个连通块，是判断蓝色极大连通块的核心拓扑规则。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae077aa7a5a85409843a4ac34869acd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61548360973c5cefdc1038d32bf69e3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bcd1771d7e55d80f714bbc3d88370bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0e2ac3fe25900f76cfe73eedcd9570d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e8858aadef99b81cf3431326cb24cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;共边&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"共边指两个砖块在上下或左右方向上共享一条边，用于判断蓝色极大连通块是否与灰色砖块直接接触，从而决定其是否可掉落。"&lt;SEP&gt;"共边是指两个砖块在上下左右方向上共享一条边，用于判断蓝色极大连通块是否与灰色砖块直接接触，决定其是否能自然掉落。"&lt;SEP&gt;"共边是指两个砖块在上下左右方向上直接相邻共享一条边，用于判断蓝色极大连通块是否与灰色砖块接触，从而决定其是否可掉落。"&lt;SEP&gt;"共边是指两个砖块在网格中共享一条边，用于判断蓝色极大连通块是否与灰色砖块接触，从而决定其是否可掉落。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bcd1771d7e55d80f714bbc3d88370bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0e2ac3fe25900f76cfe73eedcd9570d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61548360973c5cefdc1038d32bf69e3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e8858aadef99b81cf3431326cb24cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;边界上的蓝色极大连通块&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"边界上的蓝色极大连通块是指位于矩阵边缘的蓝色连通区域，其掉落条件特殊，无需考虑悬空，仅需切断与灰色砖块的共边连接。"&lt;SEP&gt;"边界上的蓝色极大连通块是指至少有一个蓝色砖块位于 n×m 矩阵的边缘，此类连通块无需考虑悬空问题，掉落条件更宽松，是问题中的特殊情形。"&lt;SEP&gt;"边界上的蓝色极大连通块是指至少有一个蓝色砖块位于矩阵的最外层行或列，这类连通块的掉落条件特殊，无需考虑悬空问题。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bcd1771d7e55d80f714bbc3d88370bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae077aa7a5a85409843a4ac34869acd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e8858aadef99b81cf3431326cb24cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;敲碎&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"敲碎是指移除灰色砖块的操作，是实现蓝色极大连通块掉落的唯一手段，其最小数量是问题的求解目标。"&lt;SEP&gt;"敲碎是指移除灰色砖块的操作，是实现蓝色极大连通块脱离的唯一手段，其最小次数是问题的求解目标。"&lt;SEP&gt;"敲碎是指移除灰色砖块的操作，是触发蓝色极大连通块掉落的必要动作，是解题的核心操作。"&lt;SEP&gt;"敲碎是指移除灰色砖块的操作，是实现蓝色极大连通块掉落的唯一手段，问题要求最小化该操作次数。"&lt;SEP&gt;"敲碎是指移除灰色砖块的操作，是触发蓝色极大连通块掉落的唯一手段，问题要求计算最少敲碎次数以实现目标。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae077aa7a5a85409843a4ac34869acd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61548360973c5cefdc1038d32bf69e3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bcd1771d7e55d80f714bbc3d88370bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0e2ac3fe25900f76cfe73eedcd9570d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e8858aadef99b81cf3431326cb24cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;悬空&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"悬空是指蓝色极大连通块边缘缺乏下方支撑，但在边界上的蓝色块不因悬空而要求额外敲碎，是边界情况的特殊处理规则。"&lt;SEP&gt;"悬空是指蓝色砖块下方或周围缺乏支撑而可能自然掉落的状态，但对于边界上的蓝色极大连通块，此状态被忽略，不作为掉落条件。"&lt;SEP&gt;"悬空是指蓝色砖块下方无支撑，但在边界情况下被忽略，是判断连通块是否稳定掉落的非关键因素，仅在非边界情况下影响分析。"&lt;SEP&gt;"悬空是指蓝色砖块在未被支撑的情况下悬挂在矩阵中，但边界上的蓝色极大连通块不考虑此状态，是规则中的例外条件。"&lt;SEP&gt;"悬空是指蓝色砖块下方或周围缺乏支撑，但在边界上的蓝色极大连通块被特别豁免此条件，是判断掉落条件的例外规则。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae077aa7a5a85409843a4ac34869acd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61548360973c5cefdc1038d32bf69e3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bcd1771d7e55d80f714bbc3d88370bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0e2ac3fe25900f76cfe73eedcd9570d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e8858aadef99b81cf3431326cb24cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STUDENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A student who submitted an incorrect answer to a programming problem involving mathematical computation with variables Min, Cnt, x, and y."&lt;SEP&gt;"An unidentified individual who submitted an incorrect answer to a problem involving a BFS algorithm implementation, likely in a programming or competitive coding context."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student is the individual who submitted an incorrect solution to a computational problem involving grid traversal and BFS, as indicated by the error description referencing Record ID 63-1."&lt;SEP&gt;"An individual whose answer was evaluated and found to be incorrect, likely a learner in an educational or automated grading context."&lt;SEP&gt;"An unnamed student who submitted an incorrect answer to a programming problem involving matrix logic and flag conditions, as indicated by the error description."&lt;SEP&gt;"An unnamed student who submitted an incorrect solution involving a code logic error related to matrix traversal and condition checking, likely in a programming or algorithmic context."&lt;SEP&gt;"An individual who submitted an incorrect solution to a programming problem involving array logic and conditional checks, likely a learner in an educational setting."&lt;SEP&gt;"A student who submitted an incorrect answer to a programming problem involving matrix logic and condition checks, as recorded in an educational system."&lt;SEP&gt;"An unnamed student who submitted an incorrect solution to a programming problem involving array manipulation and conditional logic, as indicated by the error description."&lt;SEP&gt;"An unnamed student who submitted an incorrect solution involving array manipulation and conditional logic, likely in a programming assignment or competition context."&lt;SEP&gt;"An individual submitting a coding solution in an educational assessment system, whose answer contains logical errors in matrix traversal logic."&lt;SEP&gt;"An unnamed student who submitted an incorrect solution to a programming problem involving array validation logic, flagged in an error record with timestamp and ID."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c79d0a874a6ba47efd4742ec70c1e196&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c04c2481dfa06e8cc96fafb3eb40ca4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4655c44a0c410e0c718d92b308d741b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ae1fc917022eddc74e2fec3c8d34bb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f02234c0d5217769809ae214a58779b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c43422d516179991d5c796063c71f443&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe255a1fe76c6cdfb705f9ea60c587de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1446a315ea545061645e2e34bdaaffae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7effc3a8936d5e21e04e38b0253505c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffffe6b4389bb3df97140e17e088aa9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d353b59db67cab15706b3f74c4fa457&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e307f6e0f75e0c72f6c263b74efaa1f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;61-1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An organizational or system identifier for a record tracking errors in student submissions, possibly from an automated grading or learning management system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5d353b59db67cab15706b3f74c4fa457</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BFS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BFS (Breadth-First Search) is an algorithmic event used to traverse a grid, count connected components of value 1, and track adjacent zero cells, with logic implemented in the provided code."&lt;SEP&gt;"Breadth-First Search, a graph traversal algorithm used in the code to explore connected components in a grid, counting valid cells and adjacent zero cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"bfs（广度优先搜索）是程序中用于遍历和识别蓝色极大连通块的算法，通过队列逐层探索相邻蓝色砖块。"&lt;SEP&gt;"BFS（广度优先搜索）是学生程序中使用的算法，用于系统性地探索从数字n到数字m的所有可能操作路径。"&lt;SEP&gt;"bfs 是学生程序中定义的广度优先搜索函数，用于探索从数字n到m的所有可能操作路径，是程序逻辑的核心组件，但因语法错误无法正常运行。"&lt;SEP&gt;"BFS（广度优先搜索）是学生程序中用于判断数字n能否通过指定操作变为数字m的算法策略，是解决问题的核心计算方法。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-180c6e0fe94889fc71026468d48a172f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c22dbdf1f3163e7e66ae88a5409cc589&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0e2ac3fe25900f76cfe73eedcd9570d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c43422d516179991d5c796063c71f443&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ffc536726735c9911cd4a90d2ddb49f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d353b59db67cab15706b3f74c4fa457</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An array defining the horizontal displacement for four-directional movement (right, left, up, down) in the grid during BFS traversal."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5d353b59db67cab15706b3f74c4fa457</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An array defining the vertical displacement for four-directional movement (right, left, up, down) in the grid during BFS traversal."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5d353b59db67cab15706b3f74c4fa457</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A 2D boolean array used to track visited cells during BFS traversal to prevent revisiting and cycles."&lt;SEP&gt;"VIS is a 2D array used to track visited cells during the BFS traversal, acting as a state management component within the computational system."&lt;SEP&gt;"vis 是学生程序中用于标记字符是否已出现的布尔数组，用于模拟不连续子序列检测，但逻辑错误导致结果不准确。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-34b609ebf637b7a586a64207000b2d2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d353b59db67cab15706b3f74c4fa457&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c43422d516179991d5c796063c71f443</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CNT1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A counter variable tracking the number of traversable (1) cells in the current connected component during BFS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5d353b59db67cab15706b3f74c4fa457</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CNT2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A counter variable tracking the number of adjacent zero (0) cells surrounding the current connected component during BFS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5d353b59db67cab15706b3f74c4fa457</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANS1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A variable storing the maximum size of any connected component found so far in the grid during BFS iterations."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANS1 is a global variable storing the maximum size of connected components of 1s found during BFS iterations, used for result comparison."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5d353b59db67cab15706b3f74c4fa457&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c43422d516179991d5c796063c71f443</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A variable or placeholder in a computational algorithm, likely representing a minimum value used in a mathematical expression to calculate the expected result."&lt;SEP&gt;"A variable storing the minimum number of surrounding zero cells among all connected components of maximum size, used to determine optimal solution."&lt;SEP&gt;"MIN is a global variable storing the minimum count of adjacent zero cells (cnt2) among all connected components of maximum size, used for optimization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Min 是学生程序中用于存储最少敲碎砖块数量的变量名，代表程序计算的目标输出值，是程序逻辑的核心输出。"&lt;SEP&gt;"Min is a variable in a programming expression, likely representing a minimum value used in a mathematical computation involving count and scaling factors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-61548360973c5cefdc1038d32bf69e3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4655c44a0c410e0c718d92b308d741b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c43422d516179991d5c796063c71f443&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d353b59db67cab15706b3f74c4fa457&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e307f6e0f75e0c72f6c263b74efaa1f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;砖块矩阵&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"砖块矩阵是一个 n × m 的二维网格结构，用于表示砖块的排列，其中每个位置 (i,j) 对应一个砖块，分为可敲碎的灰色砖块和不可敲碎的蓝色砖块，是问题的物理和逻辑载体。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bcd1771d7e55d80f714bbc3d88370bd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N × M 矩阵&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"n × m 矩阵是砖块的二维排布结构，用于定义砖块位置(i,j)，是问题建模和算法处理的基础空间框架。"&lt;SEP&gt;"n × m 矩阵是问题中砖块排列的总体结构，n 表示行数，m 表示列数，定义了问题的规模和空间边界，是所有分析的底层框架。"</data>
