    <node id="&quot;INT N = RAND(), M = N - (RAND() % 26 + 1)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This code snippet is an erroneous initialization of n and m using random values, which violates the problem's requirement to read n and m from input, leading to incorrect behavior."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7638980c6db214619f264bda3c98a5b8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STD::MIN(0LL , 2 * M - N)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"cnt is computed using this expression, which always evaluates to 0 due to the min with 0ll, making the logic for repeating 'a' characters invalid and non-functional."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7638980c6db214619f264bda3c98a5b8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VIS[I]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"vis[i] is a boolean array used to mark positions of repeated characters in the string, but its logic is flawed due to bidirectional scanning and incorrect update of ans."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7638980c6db214619f264bda3c98a5b8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;F[S[I]]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"f is a map used to track character occurrences for detecting repeats, but its usage is inconsistent between forward and backward passes, corrupting the final ans calculation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7638980c6db214619f264bda3c98a5b8</data>
