    <node id="&quot;ABSOLUTE EXPECTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Absolute Expectation is the mathematical event or problem centered on computing the expected value of the sum of absolute differences between consecutive elements in a randomly generated integer sequence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Absolute Expectation refers to the mathematical problem of computing the expected value of val(a), the sum of absolute differences in a randomly generated sequence, as posed in the problem titled 'Tokitsukaze and Absolute Expectation'."&lt;SEP&gt;"Absolute Expectation is the name of a mathematical problem or competition task where the goal is to compute the expected value of the absolute difference sum of a randomly generated integer sequence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Absolute Expectation is the mathematical event or problem instance where the expected value of the absolute difference sum of a randomly generated sequence is computed, as posed in the problem titled 'Tokitsukaze and Absolute Expectation'."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f207867e95527d1c21eb90640d585ef3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8c9f94da5a947d7ca0394b058d44d06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a6cf2c1b884640bd458e20b236729e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52425facb0b31d12436db806ca0992de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;L[I]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"L[i] represents the lower bound of the interval [l_i, r_i] from which the i-th element a_i of the sequence is randomly generated."&lt;SEP&gt;"L[i] represents the lower bound of the random integer range for the i-th element in the sequence, used in the computation of expected absolute differences."&lt;SEP&gt;"L[i] represents the lower bound of the random integer range for the i-th element in the sequence, defining the domain from which each a_i is uniformly sampled."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f207867e95527d1c21eb90640d585ef3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8c9f94da5a947d7ca0394b058d44d06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52425facb0b31d12436db806ca0992de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;R[I]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"R[i] represents the upper bound of the interval [l_i, r_i] from which the i-th element a_i of the sequence is randomly generated."&lt;SEP&gt;"R[i] represents the upper bound of the random integer range for the i-th element in the sequence, used in the computation of expected absolute differences."&lt;SEP&gt;"R[i] represents the upper bound of the random integer range for the i-th element in the sequence, defining the upper limit of the domain from which each a_i is uniformly sampled."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f207867e95527d1c21eb90640d585ef3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8c9f94da5a947d7ca0394b058d44d06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52425facb0b31d12436db806ca0992de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VAL(A)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"val(a) is the computed value of the sequence defined as the sum of absolute differences between consecutive elements, i.e., ∑|a_{i-1} - a_i| for i from 2 to n, which is the quantity whose expectation is sought."&lt;SEP&gt;"val(a) is the event or computed quantity defined as the sum of absolute differences between consecutive elements in the sequence, i.e., ∑|a_{i-1} - a_i| for i from 2 to n."&lt;SEP&gt;"val(a) is the mathematical function defined as the sum of absolute differences between consecutive elements in the sequence, i.e., ∑|a_{i-1} - a_i| for i from 2 to n."&lt;SEP&gt;"val(a) is the defined mathematical function representing the total absolute difference between consecutive elements in the sequence, i.e., sum_{i=2}^n |a_{i-1} - a_i|, which is the quantity whose expectation is being computed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-52425facb0b31d12436db806ca0992de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8c9f94da5a947d7ca0394b058d44d06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a6cf2c1b884640bd458e20b236729e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-643a1dae351fde67dd0b6b4bafe4269b</data>
    </node>
