    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TIC-TAC-TOE GAME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The tic-tac-toe game is a 3x3 board game between 小L and 炸鸡, where the goal is to get three of one's marks in a row, column, or diagonal. The game is in a drawn state with equal moves made, and it is now 小L's turn with a special two-move privilege."&lt;SEP&gt;"The tic-tac-toe game is a 3x3 grid-based strategic contest between 小L and 炸鸡, where the goal is to align three of one's marks in a row, column, or diagonal; the game is currently in a drawn state with equal moves and 小L is next to play with a special double-move privilege."&lt;SEP&gt;"The tic-tac-toe game is a 3x3 grid-based strategic contest between 小L and 炸鸡, where the goal is to get three of one's marks in a row, column, or diagonal. The game is in a mid-state with equal moves made by both players and no winner yet, and it is now 小L's turn with a special double-move privilege."&lt;SEP&gt;"The tic-tac-toe game is in a mid-game state with equal moves by both players, no winner yet, and it is now小L's turn with a one-time privilege to make two moves in a single turn."&lt;SEP&gt;The Tic-Tac-Toe Game is a 3x3 grid-based strategic contest between 小L and 炸鸡, where the objective is to be the first to align three of one’s marks in a row, column, or diagonal. The game is currently in a drawn state, with both players having made an equal number of moves and no winner yet determined. It is now 小L’s turn to play, and 小L possesses a special one-time privilege to make a double move—allowing two consecutive moves in a single turn. This unique rule modifies standard tic-tac-toe gameplay and provides 小L with a strategic advantage to break the current stalemate. All descriptions consistently agree on the board size, players, win condition, current drawn state, equal move count, and 小L’s double-move privilege, with no contradictions to resolve.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c65c413a0785f44cfb35456d545b19d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-649cc18b2d0fdb15683c43c49f191a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-054c255dec239c2762b373ecc1e4a1e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dc16b5f321438c090a3a2ab6291f38f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf315318fb9435781f726121555b7204&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b256fd1c0676b66deece8e4e49ff37e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f761857c7438d0e8234494cb00c030e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d34feb8b38494b33de0e8d583302bc5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a376d30d059b09f44ce6681d11e112d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea15e123e23c10fb0dd1d2aa46c0de25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65da65cd36531d031db5b8f1d3d85dab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;3X3 GRID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 3x3 grid is the playing board of the tic-tac-toe game, consisting of nine cells identified by coordinates (i,j), where i is the row (1 to 3) and j is the column (1 to 3). Each cell can contain 'X', 'O', or 'G' representing player marks or empty spaces."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 3x3 grid is the playing board of the tic-tac-toe game, consisting of nine cells identified by coordinates (i,j), where i is the row (1-3) and j is the column (1-3). Each cell can contain 'X', 'O', or 'G' representing player moves or empty spaces."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 3x3 grid is the playing board of the tic-tac-toe game, consisting of nine cells identified by coordinates (i,j), where i is the row (1–3) and j is the column (1–3). Each cell can hold 'X', 'O', or 'G' to represent moves or empty spaces."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 3x3 grid is the playing field of the tic-tac-toe game, consisting of 9 cells arranged in 3 rows and 3 columns, identified by coordinates (i,j), where i and j range from 1 to 3."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 3x3 grid is the playing field of the tic-tac-toe game, consisting of 9 cells arranged in 3 rows and 3 columns, where players place their marks to achieve three in a line."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c65c413a0785f44cfb35456d545b19d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-649cc18b2d0fdb15683c43c49f191a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fbf67613a3aed791c8801433f136cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d34feb8b38494b33de0e8d583302bc5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea15e123e23c10fb0dd1d2aa46c0de25</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;O&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"'O' is the symbol used to represent moves made by 炸鸡 on the 3x3 grid, indicating ownership of a cell in the tic-tac-toe game."&lt;SEP&gt;The symbol "O" represents the mark placed by 炸鸡 on the 3x3 tic-tac-toe board, indicating ownership of a cell and signifying one of the two player symbols used to track progress toward winning the game. "O" is specifically associated with 炸鸡 as their designated token, used to occupy one of the nine grid positions during play. While some descriptions incorrectly refer to "O" as representing an "opponent's move," this is inconsistent with the consistent attribution of "O" to 炸鸡 across the majority of descriptions. The correct interpretation is that "O" is 炸鸡’s own symbol—typically representing the second player in standard tic-tac-toe conventions—and is used to form a winning line of three aligned symbols. Thus, "O" is not an opponent’s mark but rather 炸鸡’s personal identifier on the board, essential for claiming cells and achieving victory.&lt;SEP&gt;"'O' represents the symbol placed by 炸鸡 on the 3x3 tic-tac-toe board, indicating a cell occupied by 炸鸡's move."&lt;SEP&gt;"'O' represents the symbol placed by 炸鸡 on the 3x3 board, indicating one of their moves in the game."&lt;SEP&gt;"'O' represents a mark placed by 炸鸡 on the tic-tac-toe board, indicating one of the opponent's moves in the current game state."&lt;SEP&gt;"'O' represents a mark placed by 炸鸡 on the tic-tac-toe board, indicating ownership of a cell in the 3x3 grid. It is one of two player symbols used to track progress toward winning."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-649cc18b2d0fdb15683c43c49f191a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf315318fb9435781f726121555b7204&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-031bf50845b77cce37dae6bb7e48b3a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a625df4ed1e048ecc8681beebcec0a9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b256fd1c0676b66deece8e4e49ff37e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fbf67613a3aed791c8801433f136cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d34feb8b38494b33de0e8d583302bc5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65da65cd36531d031db5b8f1d3d85dab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-054c255dec239c2762b373ecc1e4a1e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41bb705f581ef523c90424ea77cfe827&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9096db2ee9b817fdd4447c67ca4e24c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a376d30d059b09f44ce6681d11e112d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea15e123e23c10fb0dd1d2aa46c0de25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c65c413a0785f44cfb35456d545b19d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0414d324dc902fa7bfe392b580d12b0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dc16b5f321438c090a3a2ab6291f38f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53fc62282a1bad52fcf26a22bb1d2063&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f761857c7438d0e8234494cb00c030e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64cb9d6867521174d17ba3213df66180</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;G&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"'G' (empty) represents an unoccupied cell on the 3x3 board, indicating a position where no move has been made yet."&lt;SEP&gt;"'G' represents an empty cell on the 3x3 tic-tac-toe board, indicating a position where no player has placed a mark yet."&lt;SEP&gt;"'G' stands for 'empty' or 'gap' on the 3x3 grid, indicating a cell that has not yet been occupied by either player in the tic-tac-toe game."&lt;SEP&gt;G represents an empty cell on the 3x3 tic-tac-toe board, indicating a position where no player has yet placed a mark. It serves as a fundamental state indicator within the game’s grid system or grid structure, signifying available moves and contributing to the assessment of potential winning paths. The symbol "G" is synonymous with terms such as "empty" or "gap," and its presence is essential for determining the current game state, tracking unoccupied positions, and guiding strategic decision-making throughout the game. This definition is consistently supported across all descriptions, with no contradictions present.&lt;SEP&gt;"'G' represents an empty cell on the 3x3 tic-tac-toe board, indicating a position where no player has placed a mark yet."&lt;SEP&gt;"'G' represents an empty cell on the 3x3 tic-tac-toe board, indicating a position where no player has placed a mark yet. It is a state marker in the game's grid system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-649cc18b2d0fdb15683c43c49f191a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf315318fb9435781f726121555b7204&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-031bf50845b77cce37dae6bb7e48b3a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a625df4ed1e048ecc8681beebcec0a9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b256fd1c0676b66deece8e4e49ff37e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fbf67613a3aed791c8801433f136cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d34feb8b38494b33de0e8d583302bc5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65da65cd36531d031db5b8f1d3d85dab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-054c255dec239c2762b373ecc1e4a1e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41bb705f581ef523c90424ea77cfe827&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9096db2ee9b817fdd4447c67ca4e24c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a376d30d059b09f44ce6681d11e112d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea15e123e23c10fb0dd1d2aa46c0de25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c65c413a0785f44cfb35456d545b19d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0414d324dc902fa7bfe392b580d12b0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dc16b5f321438c090a3a2ab6291f38f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53fc62282a1bad52fcf26a22bb1d2063&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f761857c7438d0e8234494cb00c030e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64cb9d6867521174d17ba3213df66180</data>
