    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLAG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"'flag' is a boolean variable used to indicate whether a global condition (e.g., all rows and columns meet certain criteria) has been satisfied, likely determining the correctness of a solution."&lt;SEP&gt;"A boolean variable set to 1 when no elements exceed 1 in a specific diagonal check, indicating a successful condition pass."&lt;SEP&gt;"A boolean variable that, when set to 1, indicates a successful condition where no elements violate the specified constraints (e.g., all elements ≤ 1)."&lt;SEP&gt;"A boolean variable that, when set to 1, indicates the matrix satisfies certain conditions, serving as the final correctness indicator."</data>
