    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIAGONAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A diagonal in the tic-tac-toe game refers to one of the two lines of three cells connecting opposite corners: top-left to bottom-right, or top-right to bottom-left; completing a diagonal with three identical marks wins the game."&lt;SEP&gt;"A diagonal is a line of three cells running from corner to corner in the 3x3 grid; completing either of the two diagonals with three identical marks (X or O) results in a win."&lt;SEP&gt;"A diagonal refers to one of the two winning lines in tic-tac-toe: from top-left to bottom-right or top-right to bottom-left, where three identical marks must align to win."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2fbf67613a3aed791c8801433f136cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c65c413a0785f44cfb35456d545b19d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a625df4ed1e048ecc8681beebcec0a9e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A row in the tic-tac-toe game is a horizontal line of three cells in the 3x3 grid; completing any row with three identical marks wins the game."&lt;SEP&gt;"A row is a horizontal line of three cells in the 3x3 grid; completing a row with three identical marks (X or O) results in a win."&lt;SEP&gt;"A row is a horizontal line of three cells in the tic-tac-toe board; three identical marks in a row constitute a winning condition."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2fbf67613a3aed791c8801433f136cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c65c413a0785f44cfb35456d545b19d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a625df4ed1e048ecc8681beebcec0a9e</data>
