    <edge source="&quot;小红&quot;" target="&quot;STUDENT PROGRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d3">236.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"小红 is the problem designer, and the Student Program is an attempted solution to her defined problem of transforming a matrix into a 好矩阵."&lt;SEP&gt;"小红 is the problem setter whose '好矩阵' definition the Student Program attempts to implement, making the program a direct attempt to solve her posed challenge."&lt;SEP&gt;The Student Program is a computational solution developed as an attempted implementation of a problem defined by 小红, establishing a clear problem-solution relationship between her and the program. 小红 is the problem setter and conceptual originator who articulated the requirement for transforming an input array into a “好矩阵” (good matrix), also referred to as a “好数组” (good array) or “双生数组” (twin array), with the specific objective of minimizing the array’s range through the algorithmic transformation of doubling a subarray. Her problem constitutes a determinant construction or transformation challenge, designed to test the correctness of algorithmic reasoning in array manipulation.

The Student Program was created by a learner—likely a student or peer—as a direct response to 小红’s defined criteria, aiming to satisfy the transformation rules she established. Despite being explicitly aligned with her problem specification, the program contains logical and implementation errors that prevent it from correctly producing a valid “好矩阵.” As a result, it fails to meet the functional requirements set forth by 小红, and its output is evaluated as incorrect. While some descriptions may ambiguously suggest 小红 could be the program’s author or user, the consistent and dominant thread across all inputs confirms that she is not the implementer but rather the designer of the problem. The program, therefore, represents an external, imperfect attempt by another party to solve her challenge.

In summary, 小红 is the authoritative source of the problem, defining the target transformation and correctness criteria, while the Student Program is an erroneous, learner-generated solution that, despite its intent, fails to correctly implement the required algorithmic transformation. Their relationship is unambiguously that of problem designer and attempted solver, with the program’s failure highlighting the gap between conceptual specification and correct execution.&lt;SEP&gt;"小红 poses the problem that the Student Program attempts to solve, making the program a direct response to her defined criteria for a '好矩阵'."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-5a0e68ffe11c5d605b2d172bc117a660&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eeffa4db6e2444dac981d2f6e46c8e68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5e545f02779dfb717361dfc31cb72c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7907aaf6e77e8266bb40e1c8a136bf60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72507ce11e78cbb0f5fe85180ed22a32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e3f9d595e0b4dc6b94e1564563f7ded&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47e1da39547e4d5d5cdafb2530c061c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-466772e1ad2cb9b8fdd70bf09c71858c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad8afc7ac300d86b72e962805041fa5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fe6cf8d6835af29afa5ade64370e360&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24e91156da41d8c127cfcd98fd99217c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e118fc6033f61b8968a68a6cbe21cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2a57305752e3a687103dd58dbee53bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e9ce81e31f65b60ba40e243a8d1ba19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70a2665d10418a7ca4b53ae850057cff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de530eec1b33d2199269b22b88bb1c32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35ba454db150409dfa2569afe0680c61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-504efc1d29aab22b90705499f57173fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-264071873a8220efc52cdb3c6f973f1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7230c75a37c25448800f6f28d89050f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46766da85f9f13835e435950173174a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-802a483142e00c23622efad16d2e5519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3eac5a8ba5cac7de40889ced9fb5315&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8af7cfb62173340e7ef202c51be3c0d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e091fd25a6ba2509fa168c85c52636ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0c9c6802989382170739955a5bae46c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2ac191ac64f16e456c655d4b8863811&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-468ecda2a7ffd84f7956eab9b179bd56</data>
