      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"n定义了问题的规模，决定操作的可能组合数和搜索空间，是算法设计的基础。"</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-57add46cc4c97ae41d878b651704f581</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;N&quot;" target="&quot;A[I][J]&quot;">
      <data key="d3">18.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The variable n defines the dimension of the matrix a[i][j], determining the bounds for all nested loops and index ranges."&lt;SEP&gt;"The variable n defines the dimensions of the matrix a[i][j], determining the bounds for all nested loops and array accesses."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-c79d0a874a6ba47efd4742ec70c1e196&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f02234c0d5217769809ae214a58779b</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;N&quot;" target="&quot;A[K][3 - K + 1]&quot;">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The matrix size 'n' defines the range over which a[k][3 - k + 1] is accessed, making it essential for correct indexing."&lt;SEP&gt;"The variable n defines the bounds of the loop that accesses the anti-diagonal elements a[k][3 - k + 1], making it essential to the expression’s correctness."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-7effc3a8936d5e21e04e38b0253505c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffffe6b4389bb3df97140e17e088aa9b</data>
