    <edge source="&quot;STUDENT PROGRAM&quot;" target="&quot;GCD&quot;">
      <data key="d3">19.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The Student Program does not correctly implement gcd logic, leading to errors in validating the condition a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Student Program uses gcd conceptually by iterating over divisors of a[i], but does not explicitly compute gcd(a_i, a_j), leading to logical errors."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Student Program implicitly relies on gcd computation, but does not correctly implement or verify the condition linking gcd and xor."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-91d5ad5a52520d2ee66b7e8855842a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54e2ed195b50756e6f2448b5f990c4b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9bb8ae3fef264eb1654019ea7fdabc</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;STUDENT PROGRAM&quot;" target="&quot;XOR&quot;">
      <data key="d3">21.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The Student Program uses XOR operation in its logic to compare values, but fails to correctly validate all valid (a_i, a_j) pairs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Student Program uses xor implicitly via the ^ operator in C++, but fails to correctly account for its behavior in relation to gcd."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Student Program uses xor operation in the condition (a[i] ^ j) to test potential matches, but incorrectly assumes j is a_j rather than a divisor."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-91d5ad5a52520d2ee66b7e8855842a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54e2ed195b50756e6f2448b5f990c4b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9bb8ae3fef264eb1654019ea7fdabc</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
