    <edge source="&quot;X&quot;" target="&quot;Y&quot;">
      <data key="d3">20.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"x 和 y 是两种操作的成本参数，它们的相对大小决定了是选择翻转还是交换操作更经济，直接影响最小花费的计算策略。"&lt;SEP&gt;"x和y是两种操作的成本参数，它们的相对大小决定了最优策略是使用翻转（x*Cnt）还是交换（y*交换次数）来最小化总花费。"</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-c32b07be1497200073fc0ef9c06b5453&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aec8259c8baec36c3dade3722427d1e1</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;X&quot;" target="&quot;小L&quot;">
      <data key="d3">180.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"小L places 'X' marks on the board during their turns, making 'X' the symbolic representation of their moves in the game."&lt;SEP&gt;"小L uses the 'X' symbol to mark their moves on the tic-tac-toe board."&lt;SEP&gt;X is the symbol used by 小L to mark their moves on the tic-tac-toe board, directly representing 小L’s actions, ownership, and identity within the game. Across multiple descriptions, it is consistently affirmed that 小L employs the 'X' symbol as their exclusive marker to denote plays on the tic-tac-toe grid, establishing a clear and direct association between the player and their game piece. This usage not only signifies whose turn it is or whose move has been made but also serves as an emblem of personal agency and control in the game.

Additionally, in a separate but related context, 小L’s strategic decision-making in an operational or computational setting is influenced by a variable denoted as 'x', which determines the cost of flipping a single bit in entities 'a' or 'b'. This 'x' functions as a critical cost parameter in 小L’s optimization process, affecting how they choose actions to minimize expenditure. While the symbol 'X' in the tic-tac-toe context is a visual marker of play, the variable 'x' in the cost model is an abstract numerical or computational parameter—distinct in nature but phonetically and orthographically identical. The two uses of 'X'/'x' refer to different domains: one is a game symbol, the other a cost variable in a decision-making framework.

Thus, while the descriptions concerning the tic-tac-toe board are fully consistent and reinforce each other, the references to 'x' as a cost variable introduce a separate, non-contradictory layer of meaning: the same symbol, 'X'/'x', operates in two distinct contexts—game representation and operational optimization—both central to 小L’s behavior, but not interchangeable. In summary: 小L uses 'X' as their iconic marker in tic-tac-toe to represent their moves and ownership, while simultaneously relying on a cost variable 'x' to optimize their strategic decisions in a computational or operational environment.&lt;SEP&gt;"小L uses the 'X' symbol to mark their moves on the tic-tac-toe board, establishing direct ownership and gameplay identity."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-649cc18b2d0fdb15683c43c49f191a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf315318fb9435781f726121555b7204&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-031bf50845b77cce37dae6bb7e48b3a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a625df4ed1e048ecc8681beebcec0a9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b256fd1c0676b66deece8e4e49ff37e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fbf67613a3aed791c8801433f136cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5eb1d8406f1c61b5ad1590b8396b2ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d34feb8b38494b33de0e8d583302bc5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65da65cd36531d031db5b8f1d3d85dab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c32b07be1497200073fc0ef9c06b5453&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-054c255dec239c2762b373ecc1e4a1e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41bb705f581ef523c90424ea77cfe827&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9096db2ee9b817fdd4447c67ca4e24c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a376d30d059b09f44ce6681d11e112d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea15e123e23c10fb0dd1d2aa46c0de25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c65c413a0785f44cfb35456d545b19d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0414d324dc902fa7bfe392b580d12b0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dc16b5f321438c090a3a2ab6291f38f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f761857c7438d0e8234494cb00c030e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64cb9d6867521174d17ba3213df66180</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
