    <edge source="&quot;(I,J)&quot;" target="&quot;TOKITSUKAZE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Tokitsukaze selects any coordinate (i,j) on the grid map to unleash Dragon's Breath, making (i,j) the target of her action."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-89dd6bd1e7fef4152822627f117d0a69</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;(I,J)&quot;" target="&quot;GRID MAP&quot;">
      <data key="d3">39.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"(i,j) is the coordinate system that precisely identifies each cell within the Grid Map, forming the spatial basis for monster placement and Dragon's Breath targeting."&lt;SEP&gt;"(i,j) is the coordinate system that structures the Grid Map, enabling precise location of monsters and flame propagation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Grid Map is defined by coordinates (i,j), which uniquely identify each cell containing monster counts a_{i,j}."&lt;SEP&gt;"(i,j) is the coordinate system used to index every cell in the grid map, forming the spatial structure of the battlefield."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-411bbe91994001030c7a545311f4d2a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ab3ebf5f1287dbbf9a2ec35fad95eea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89dd6bd1e7fef4152822627f117d0a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d793d3b341bfc53e485a1d35351f539</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;(I,J)&quot;" target="&quot;DRAGON'S BREATH&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Dragon's Breath is activated at a specific (i,j) coordinate on the grid map, which determines the center of the X-shaped flame pattern."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-325b730cedcf46c053439807511ce0ee</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;(I,J)&quot;" target="&quot;A_{I,J}&quot;">
      <data key="d3">10.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"a_{i,j} is the monster count directly associated with the grid cell identified by coordinate (i,j), forming the core data of the problem."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-d177fa42f88e3250bf9921ff21987ec2</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;(I,J)&quot;" target="&quot;S_{I,J}&quot;">
      <data key="d3">50.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"(i,j) is the coordinate index that defines the location for which s_{i,j} reports the state (X, O, or G)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The coordinate (i,j) is used to index and reference the state variable s_{i,j}, defining the exact position on the board whose state is being recorded."&lt;SEP&gt;"(i,j) is the coordinate that indexes the state variable s_{i,j}, defining the exact location and content of each cell in the tic-tac-toe grid."&lt;SEP&gt;"(i,j) is the coordinate that indexes the state variable s_{i,j}, forming the structural foundation of the board representation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The coordinate (i,j) directly references the state variable s_{i,j}, defining the location and content of each cell in the game grid."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-0414d324dc902fa7bfe392b580d12b0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41bb705f581ef523c90424ea77cfe827&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64cb9d6867521174d17ba3213df66180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9096db2ee9b817fdd4447c67ca4e24c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-031bf50845b77cce37dae6bb7e48b3a8</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;(I,J)&quot;" target="&quot;G&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"'G' is the state value assigned to cell (i,j) when it is unoccupied, defining the available positions for future moves."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-41bb705f581ef523c90424ea77cfe827</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;(I,J)&quot;" target="&quot;THREE-IN-A-ROW&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The coordinate system (i,j) defines the positions that must be occupied to achieve a three-in-a-row win condition in rows, columns, or diagonals."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-64cb9d6867521174d17ba3213df66180</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;四连通&quot;" target="&quot;边界上的蓝色极大连通块&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"边界上的蓝色极大连通块同样遵循四连通规则，只是其位置在矩阵边界，导致掉落条件简化。"</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-ae077aa7a5a85409843a4ac34869acd1</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;边界上的蓝色极大连通块&quot;" target="&quot;悬空&quot;">
      <data key="d3">22.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"悬空是普通蓝色极大连通块的考虑因素，但边界上的蓝色极大连通块被明确排除对此的考虑，形成规则例外。"&lt;SEP&gt;"悬空概念在边界上的蓝色极大连通块中被明确忽略，说明其在该情形下不影响掉落判定，二者存在逻辑排除关系。"&lt;SEP&gt;"边界上的蓝色极大连通块被特别允许忽略悬空状态，悬空在此类情况下不构成掉落障碍，是题目设定的例外规则。"</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-0bcd1771d7e55d80f714bbc3d88370bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae077aa7a5a85409843a4ac34869acd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e8858aadef99b81cf3431326cb24cb</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;边界上的蓝色极大连通块&quot;" target="&quot;掉落&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"边界上的蓝色极大连通块的掉落不依赖于悬空状态，仅需切断与灰色砖块的连接，是掉落规则的特殊情形。"</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-ae077aa7a5a85409843a4ac34869acd1</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;敲碎&quot;" target="&quot;掉落&quot;">
      <data key="d3">10.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"敲碎灰色砖块是触发蓝色极大连通块掉落的必要条件，二者存在直接因果关系。"</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-ae077aa7a5a85409843a4ac34869acd1</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;悬空&quot;" target="&quot;边界&quot;">
      <data key="d3">14.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"悬空规则仅在非边界区域生效，边界上的蓝色块不因悬空而需要额外处理，二者构成逻辑上的互斥条件。"&lt;SEP&gt;"悬空规则在边界处被豁免，边界定义了悬空条件的适用范围，是规则例外的地理边界。"</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-a0e2ac3fe25900f76cfe73eedcd9570d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61548360973c5cefdc1038d32bf69e3c</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
